"""heard-ui: a light overlay for heard, in the spirit of Cluely. macOS, Windows, Linux (one Qt script).

A translucent, always-on-top bar that is excluded from screen sharing, with:
  - the Listening / Paused switch (capture happens only while this is on)
  - the live transcript (lines land a few seconds after someone speaks; the sentence in progress is dimmed)
  - search over the retained history
  - Assist ("what should I say next?"), Ask (a question about the conversation), Recap, answered by Claude
    over the Anthropic API with the last minutes of transcript as context: sent only when you press a button
  - Save: the transcript and the last answer as a Markdown file in your notes folder
  - a tray / menu bar icon that shows whether capture is on

Global hotkeys: ⌘⇧↩ Assist, ⌘⇧H show/hide, ⌘⇧L listening on/off (Ctrl+Shift on Windows). None on Linux.
Everything reads ~/.local/share/heard (heard.db, live.json, paused, daemon.alive); settings and the API key are in
ui-config.json there, owner-only.
"""
